(6303858, 931409, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by njsabs:</b></div><hr/><i> Adam....congrats on your ribbon.  Gorgeous image of the Santa Monica Pier....your on a roll!!!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks!  You mean, Allen :)</td>', 'Originally posted by njsabs: Adam....congrats on your ribbon.  Gorgeous image of the Santa Monica Pier....your on a roll!!!!   Thanks!  You mean, Allen :)', '2011-02-05 21:21:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(6304207, 931470, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>As a relatively new member to DPC, I suppose this is the first critique you will have received via the critique club.  I hope I do not offend you in any way, but feel free to contact me directly if you would like further feedback.<br/> <br/>We''re a tough crowd to please here on DPC. Always looking for that little bit extra.<br/> <br/>This image met the challenge, no question, however, it is missing the little bit extra I referred to above.  <br/> <br/>From a technical perspective, the centre of the hub is a little bit blown out.  A quick fix in editing software would sort this out, which I gather you may now have, but didn''t have at the time of entry.<br/> <br/>I find the composition to be a bit tight.  It may have been better to step back a bit and include the top of the wheel, giving the image a more complete feel, perhaps some context.<br/> <br/>Overall, not a bad start, but just lacking some wow factor.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club As a relatively new member to DPC, I suppose this is the first critique you will have received via the critique club.  I hope I do not offend you in any way, but feel free to contact me directly if you would like further feedback. We''re a tough crowd to please here on DPC. Always looking for that little bit extra. This image met the challenge, no question, however, it is missing the little bit extra I referred to above.   From a technical perspective, the centre of the hub is a little bit blown out.  A quick fix in editing software would sort this out, which I gather you may now have, but didn''t have at the time of entry. I find the composition to be a bit tight.  It may have been better to step back a bit and include the top of the wheel, giving the image a more complete feel, perhaps some context. Overall, not a bad start, but just lacking some wow factor. ', '2011-02-06 10:53:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6304368, 931456, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>My thoughts are very much along the lines of <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=30364" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Ubique</a>''s. The blur is wonderful and I love the shadow of the bike.<br/> <br/>For DPC though, the image probably needs a bit of a saturation and contrast boost.  This may have helped the score a little.  I may have been tempted to actually convert it to black and white.<br/> <br/>I have to confess, I find it quite hard to critique this image.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club My thoughts are very much along the lines of  Ubique''s. The blur is wonderful and I love the shadow of the bike. For DPC though, the image probably needs a bit of a saturation and contrast boost.  This may have helped the score a little.  I may have been tempted to actually convert it to black and white. I have to confess, I find it quite hard to critique this image.', '2011-02-06 15:29:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(6304766, 931211, 48115, '<td valign="top"><br/>*Hello from the Critique club*<br/> <br/>First Impression: hum.. whats going on here, some colors are a bit to bright and others a bit to bland. Some thing bugs me about the composition.<br/> <br/>Composition /Background: background looks nice what lacks in composition is probably the busyness of the image as a whole. And the fact that the pinwheel isn straigt, i think the photo needs a strong leading line<br/> <br/>Post Processing: even though the colors are a bit much, i think it''s them that give this photo its charm. I would have croped quite alot of the botom ground part so you couldn''t see where the wheel was dug in.<br/> <br/>Challenge: Out of the box ideas like this have a way of geting grumpy voters to vote even grumpyer. Im not saying go inside the box, just expect a few hars votes. <br/> <br/>Overall: A few minor issues coming together make the shot a bit photographicly awkward. Believe you me, this is not bad for a 1st enter, i think i got around 3.6 on most of my first enterys so keep them comming!<br/> <br/>I would have voted 6<br/> <br/>Happy shooting :)</td>', '*Hello from the Critique club* First Impression: hum.. whats going on here, some colors are a bit to bright and others a bit to bland. Some thing bugs me about the composition. Composition /Background: background looks nice what lacks in composition is probably the busyness of the image as a whole. And the fact that the pinwheel isn straigt, i think the photo needs a strong leading line Post Processing: even though the colors are a bit much, i think it''s them that give this photo its charm. I would have croped quite alot of the botom ground part so you couldn''t see where the wheel was dug in. Challenge: Out of the box ideas like this have a way of geting grumpy voters to vote even grumpyer. Im not saying go inside the box, just expect a few hars votes.  Overall: A few minor issues coming together make the shot a bit photographicly awkward. Believe you me, this is not bad for a 1st enter, i think i got around 3.6 on most of my first enterys so keep them comming! I would have voted 6 Happy shooting :)', '2011-02-07 00:13:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(6312814, 931470, 117474, '<td valign="top">Hmm. I liked this shot. I gave it 7. I liked the lines and curve of the wheel along with the texture of the tyre and the contrasting yellow and black. <br/> <br/>One problem is that the bright spot draws the eye to the bottom right. You must realise that this competition was titled "wheels"... which suggests that the eye should instead be drawn to the wheels in your shot. The centre of the wheel pulls me away from the black rubber every time. The yellow is at the intersection of two thirds lines, which is normally where you''d want to put your main subject for a thirds composition. I think that''s why I''m being drawn towards it. <br/>I like the tight crop. It saturates the viewer with ''wheel''... I don''t think that''s a bad thing... but I''m no great photographer :) I just like what I like and I liked that!</td>', 'Hmm. I liked this shot. I gave it 7. I liked the lines and curve of the wheel along with the texture of the tyre and the contrasting yellow and black.  One problem is that the bright spot draws the eye to the bottom right. You must realise that this competition was titled "wheels"... which suggests that the eye should instead be drawn to the wheels in your shot. The centre of the wheel pulls me away from the black rubber every time. The yellow is at the intersection of two thirds lines, which is normally where you''d want to put your main subject for a thirds composition. I think that''s why I''m being drawn towards it. I like the tight crop. It saturates the viewer with ''wheel''... I don''t think that''s a bad thing... but I''m no great photographer :) I just like what I like and I liked that!', '2011-02-14 09:55:09.000000', NULL, 0),
